---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";
import "../styles/trust.css";
---
<Base
  title="Trust · Meridian"
  description="What Meridian does to protect your data and your decisions, said plainly: only what is true today."
  share="og-trust.png"
  shareAlt="Meridian: Said plainly, and only what's true. An example access list for the DACH Workspace, with each person's role."
>

<main id="main">

<!-- 1 · Hero: words left, who has access right -->
<section class="trhero" id="top"><div class="in trhero-grid">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <span class="pill">Trust</span>
    <h1>Said plainly, <em>and only what's true.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">What Meridian does to protect your data and your decisions. If your review needs more, send us your security questionnaire.</p>
    <div class="btns"><a class="btn" href="#today">What's true today</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/request-a-walkthrough?topic=security">Send your questionnaire</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="trart mint halo" role="img" aria-label="Example access list for the DACH Workspace: Laura Whitfield as marketing manager, Samir Haddad on the claims team, and Grace Adeyemi as an approver."><span class="sheet" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <ul class="card tracc" id="tracc"><li class="fl-t">Access · DACH Workspace</li><li><i class="av a2">LW</i><span>Laura Whitfield</span><span class="st">Marketing manager</span></li><li><i class="av a4">SH</i><span>Samir Haddad</span><span class="st v">Claims team</span></li><li><i class="av a3">GA</i><span>Grace Adeyemi</span><span class="st w">Channels leader</span></li></ul>
    <div class="chip trchip"><i class="ok">✓</i>Per person, per Workspace, per role</div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 2 · True today: heading left, one accordion column right -->
<section class="sec" id="today" aria-labelledby="h-today"><div class="in acols">
  <div class="ahead"><h2 id="h-today" class="rv">True <em>today.</em></h2><p class="lead rv">Nine things you can rely on now.</p></div>
  <div class="acc">
    <details id="t-isolated" class="pv" name="tf" open><summary><h3>Your data is kept apart from every other customer's</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Each customer's data is isolated from every other customer's. <a class="lk" href="/controls#c-18">See the rule <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
    <details id="t-access" class="pv" name="tf"><summary><h3>Access is granted per person, per Workspace, per role</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Nobody gets access by default. Your program administrator invites each person and gives them a role in each Workspace.</p></div></details>
    <details id="t-staff" class="pv" name="tf"><summary><h3>Meridian staff can't open your records in the app</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Meridian staff set up your organization and have no access to your business records through the application. <a class="lk" href="/controls#c-19">See the rule <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
    <details id="t-partners" class="pv" name="tf"><summary><h3>Partners see only their own organization</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Partners never see internal notes, internal reasons, budgets or other partners. Internal reasons are kept in a separate field from the partner's explanation and are never sent to the partner. <a class="lk" href="/for-partners#sees">What partners see <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
    <details id="t-record" class="pv" name="tf"><summary><h3>Every decision is on the record</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Each decision is stored with the person, their role and the time. Each request keeps the form and approval-route version it was submitted under. <a class="lk" href="/audit-evidence-pack">See it on a record <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
    <details id="t-files" class="pv" name="tf"><summary><h3>Files can't be changed after upload</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Uploaded files cannot be altered after upload. A correction is uploaded as a new file and the original stays on the record, and each file's fingerprint would show any change.</p></div></details>
    <details id="t-money" class="pv" name="tf"><summary><h3>Meridian never moves money</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Approved invoices go to your accounts payable address, stamped with who approved them. Payment stays in your finance system. <a class="lk" href="/questions#q-paid">Do you pay our partners? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
    <details id="t-leave" class="pv" name="tf"><summary><h3>Your data leaves with you</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Nothing is deleted while your contract runs, so your audit records stay complete. When it ends, you have 30 days to get a full copy of your data. We then delete all of it within 90 days, including backups, unless the law requires us to keep something longer, and confirm the deletion in writing on request, with a deletion certificate where your contract requires one.</p></div></details>
    <details id="t-people" class="pv" name="tf"><summary><h3>A person gives every verdict</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Meridian reads cost figures from uploaded files to save typing. A person on your claims team gives the verdict on every file and every cost line. <a class="lk" href="/questions#q-ai">Do you use AI? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
  </div>
</div></section>



<!-- 3 · Check it yourself: two doors -->
<section class="sec trdoors-s" aria-labelledby="h-check"><div class="in">
  <div class="sec-c"><h2 id="h-check" class="rv">Check it <em>yourself.</em></h2></div>
  <div class="trdoors">
    <a class="trdoor rose pv" href="/controls"><h3>The controls</h3><p>Every rule the workflow enforces, in plain words.</p><span class="lk">See the controls <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a>
    <a class="trdoor butter pv" href="/audit-evidence-pack"><h3>The audit evidence pack</h3><p>One request's full history: every decision and every file.</p><span class="lk">Open the pack <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 4 · Close: one block of solid indigo -->
<section class="close" id="walkthrough" aria-labelledby="h-close"><div class="in">
  <div class="blk pv"><h2 id="h-close">Send us your<br>security questionnaire.</h2><p>We'll answer it in full, and say plainly where the answer is "not yet".</p><a class="btn white" href="/request-a-walkthrough?topic=security">Send your questionnaire</a></div>
  <ul class="qs"><li><a href="/questions">Questions</a></li><li><a href="/controls">See the controls</a></li><li><a href="/audit-evidence-pack">Open the audit evidence pack</a></li></ul>
</div></section>

</main>

<script>
  import "../scripts/trust.js";
</script>
</Base>
